# Gate/telemetry operational artifacts (local, transient)
artifacts/self-hosted/madaros
# Purpose-built rung executors (~100 MB each; claim-native, token-binding,
# witness-binding, provenance, self-falsifying). Only `madaros` was ignored, so
# five of these sat untracked and committable — 486 MB one `git add -A` away.
# They are rebuilt on demand: claim_native_gate.sh and
# self_falsifying_compiler_gate.sh call build_modular_madaros.sh into their own
# path, and the R1/R2/R17/R20 compile arms take MADAROS_RAW_BIN. The behaviour
# receipts bind self-hosted/compiler/claim_executor.sio's sha256, not the ELF,
# so deleting one costs a rebuild, never evidence.
# Keep the trailing-dot form (madaros.gate-receipt) tracked — it does not match.
artifacts/self-hosted/madaros-*
artifacts/omega/*.elf
artifacts/omega/**/*.local.json
artifacts/omega/**/*.pid
artifacts/omega/**/hourly_report.v1.jsonl
